-- title:
--   Finite flat descent of the inertia-displacement quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $R_q = \mathbb{Z}_{(q)}$ denote the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt q`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $q$. Let $H$ be a commutative ring carrying a cocommutative Hopf algebra structure over $R_q$ which is finite and flat as an $R_q$-module. Let $J$ be an additive abelian group with a distributive action of $\mathrm{Gal} = (\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[\mathbb{Q}]} \overline{\mathbb{Q}})$, let $M \le J$ be a subgroup, and let $e$ be a bijection from the convolution monoid `WithConv` of $R_q$-algebra maps $H \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ onto $M$ which turns convolution into addition ($e(f*g) = e f + e g$) and is Galois-equivariant in the sense that whenever $g = \sigma \circ f$ pointwise one has $e g = \sigma \cdot e f$ in $J$. Let $A_q$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A_q$, and let $I$ be its inertia subgroup over $\mathbb{Q}$, viewed inside $\mathrm{Gal}$ as the image of the inertia subgroup of the decomposition subgroup. Then there is a finite subset $S \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose elements lie in $A_q$ and are fixed by every element of $I$, such that for every subring $O \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $S \subseteq O \subseteq A_q$, containing the image of every rational with denominator coprime to $q$, such that $O$ is a discrete valuation ring in which $q$ is irreducible and every element of $O$ of $A_q$-valuation $< 1$ is a non-unit, the following holds: there exists a type $H'$ with a commutative ring structure and a cocommutative Hopf algebra structure over $O$, finite and flat as an $O$-module, with only finitely many $O$-algebra maps $H' \to O$, together with a bijection $e'$ from the convolution monoid of $O$-algebra maps $H' \to O$ onto the quotient of $M$ by the subgroup of $M$ induced by the subgroup of $J$ generated by all displacements $\sigma \cdot x - x$ with $\sigma \in I$ and $x \in M$, such that $e'$ carries convolution to addition and every $\varphi \in$ `WithConv` $(H \to_{R_q} \overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ admits an $x$ with $e' x$ the class of $e\varphi$, and with the additional property that if $\varphi$ is residually trivial, i.e. $\varphi(h) - \varepsilon(h)$ has $A_q$-valuation $< 1$ for all $h \in H$ (where $\varepsilon$ is the counit), then $x$ is residually trivial too, i.e. $x(h') - \varepsilon(h')$ is a non-unit of $O$ for all $h' \in H'$.
--
--   This is the Hopf-algebra form of the descent of the inertia-quotient (étale quotient) of a finite flat group scheme from the fraction field to a suitable discrete valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: the group of geometric points is replaced by its quotient by the subgroup generated by inertia displacements, which is realised as the points of a finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebra over $O$, compatibly with residual triviality. It is obtained from [`HopfAlgebra.exists_finiteFlat_quotient_of_forall_fixing_smul_mem`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_finiteFlat_quotient_of_forall_fixing_smul_mem) and feeds into [`GaloisRep.exists_finiteFlat_inertia_displacement_quotient_of_finiteFlatHopf`](thm.html#GaloisRep.exists_finiteFlat_inertia_displacement_quotient_of_finiteFlatHopf).
